tools/pipeline\matrix.html:956:Harm if reached: emulated clock frozen -- hz=0 -&gt; timer_clamp_freq floors to TIMER_MIN_FREQUENCY = 1e-8 Hz, one tick per 3.17 years. — evidence: git show 1ce189c --stat; dev_8253.c I8253_TIMER_MSB arm</span></span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="ph st-held"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Regression testing</th><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td><td class="c none"><span class="g">·</span></td></tr><tr class="fixhead st-held"><th colspan="10"><span class="hline"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="rid">m8probe</span><span class="ttl">m8probe  m8820x PROBE_USER/PROBE_SUPER are dropped, so SSR answers a deterministic miss</span><span class="tip">m8probe  m8820x PROBE_USER/PROBE_SUPER are dropped, so SSR answers a deterministic miss — HOLD: *** RE-FILED LATENT 2026-08-26 ON THE `gdrompiooddlen` PRECEDENT -- REACHABILITY MEASURED NEGATIVE, WITH CONTROLS IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. MUST NOT BE RANKED LIVE. *** A full OpenBSD 7.7/luna88k boot to `login:` (7,684,964,995 instructions) issues **seven distinct CMMU commands and ZERO probes**. Denominator stated: 0 of 7 distinct commands, not 0 of 0 -- and it independently replicates #433&#x27;s finding thirty rounds later. **The controls are what make this evidence:** a real guest supervisor store on a cold debugger, with the planted word DISASSEMBLED BEFORE STEPPING per the hand-assembled-encoding rule -- cmd 0x24 and 0x20 fire the detector, cmd 0x35 does not while still registering as M8CMD_FIRST. So the negative is real and not a broken grep. CORROBORATION that sharpens it past &#x27;this guest does not&#x27;: OpenBSD&#x27;s m88k CMMU driver issues CMMU_PROBE from exactly two places and **both are inside DDB display routines** -- a kernel-debugger feature, not an operating path, reachable only by a human at a DDB prompt. (Caveat recorded by the seat: that source is OpenBSD 2.2/mvme88k, the lineage, not the booting guest; the boot measurement is the evidence for the actual guest.) *** THE OLD COST NOTE WAS WRONG AND IS CORRECTED HERE. *** &#x27;Needs the translation walk&#x27; implies a CAPABILITY gap. **The walk exists** -- m88k_translate_v2p() at memory_m88k.c:103 -- **and is already side-effect-free under FLAG_NOEXCEPTIONS** (:344 guards the PG_U/PG_M writeback, :374 returns before any PFSR/PFAR write), its flags already cover the probe&#x27;s own selectors, and the SSR bit layout is in-tree. **And the driving probe SHAPE is already committed**: m8820x_sites_probe.py:159 ships a PROBE_SUPER row driven by one real guest instruction, ~3 s, no boot. *This is the `sh4dmacie` situation in reverse -- there the shape was missing and it was mis-read as a capability gap; here the shape was already there and nobody re-read the probe.* **WHAT IS ACTUALLY MISSING IS AN ORACLE, AND THE HOLD IS NOW CONDITIONAL ON IT:** translate_v2p exposes no BATC-vs-PATC-vs-walk distinction (needed for CMMU_SSR_BH) and none of the U/M/PROT/SO attributes SSR must carry; real probe semantics are supported only by DDB code reading those registers, which is evidence and not proof; and **there is no 88200/88204 manual in this project**. TRIGGER, on the SH4_VAL_NCLASS precedent: **if an 88200/88204 manual is obtained, this becomes a small round.** That converts an indefinite hold into a conditional one. *** AND THE CURRENT BEHAVIOUR IS THE BETTER ONE, which is the strongest reason not to rank it: *** a dropped probe leaves SSR zero with the V bit clear -- a deterministic, DEFINED &#x27;no valid translation&#x27;. Implementing without the manual would replace a defined conservative miss with an INVENTED answer that could steer the guest&#x27;s paging. **That is the same reasoning used to decline `sh4aaalias` before the SH manual arrived -- and that one turned out to be a wrong finding.** The only known consumer prints a line in a debugger display, so a cosmetically wrong DDB line for a human is the entire measured consequence. WORTH ADDING CHEAPLY: one row asserting SSR == 0 after a probe, to pin the DELIBERATE behaviour that today rests on prose in two comments and no oracle at all. — witness: none -- LATENT. The claim is true by reading, but the path is unreached by any operating guest OS, so no rung-3/4 witness can be built without first constructing a guest that probes. — note: *** EVIDENCE 2026-08-27: the claim is TRUE and the path is COMPLETELY UNREACHED by operating guest OS paths. Latent. ***
tools/pipeline\matrix.html:964:</span></span><span class="state st-held" title="*** RE-FILED LATENT 2026-08-26 ON THE `gdrompiooddlen` PRECEDENT -- REACHABILITY MEASURED NEGATIVE, WITH CONTROLS IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. MUST NOT BE RANKED LIVE. *** A full OpenBSD 7.7/luna88k boot to `login:` (7,684,964,995 instructions) issues **seven distinct CMMU commands and ZERO probes**. Denominator stated: 0 of 7 distinct commands, not 0 of 0 -- and it independently replicates #433&#x27;s finding thirty rounds later. **The controls are what make this evidence:** a real guest supervisor store on a cold debugger, with the planted word DISASSEMBLED BEFORE STEPPING per the hand-assembled-encoding rule -- cmd 0x24 and 0x20 fire the detector, cmd 0x35 does not while still registering as M8CMD_FIRST. So the negative is real and not a broken grep. CORROBORATION that sharpens it past &#x27;this guest does not&#x27;: OpenBSD&#x27;s m88k CMMU driver issues CMMU_PROBE from exactly two places and **both are inside DDB display routines** -- a kernel-debugger feature, not an operating path, reachable only by a human at a DDB prompt. (Caveat recorded by the seat: that source is OpenBSD 2.2/mvme88k, the lineage, not the booting guest; the boot measurement is the evidence for the actual guest.) *** THE OLD COST NOTE WAS WRONG AND IS CORRECTED HERE. *** &#x27;Needs the translation walk&#x27; implies a CAPABILITY gap. **The walk exists** -- m88k_translate_v2p() at memory_m88k.c:103 -- **and is already side-effect-free under FLAG_NOEXCEPTIONS** (:344 guards the PG_U/PG_M writeback, :374 returns before any PFSR/PFAR write), its flags already cover the probe&#x27;s own selectors, and the SSR bit layout is in-tree. **And the driving probe SHAPE is already committed**: m8820x_sites_probe.py:159 ships a PROBE_SUPER row driven by one real guest instruction, ~3 s, no boot. *This is the `sh4dmacie` situation in reverse -- there the shape was missing and it was mis-read as a capability gap; here the shape was already there and nobody re-read the probe.* **WHAT IS ACTUALLY MISSING IS AN ORACLE, AND THE HOLD IS NOW CONDITIONAL ON IT:** translate_v2p exposes no BATC-vs-PATC-vs-walk distinction (needed for CMMU_SSR_BH) and none of the U/M/PROT/SO attributes SSR must carry; real probe semantics are supported only by DDB code reading those registers, which is evidence and not proof; and **there is no 88200/88204 manual in this project**. TRIGGER, on the SH4_VAL_NCLASS precedent: **if an 88200/88204 manual is obtained, this becomes a small round.** That converts an indefinite hold into a conditional one. *** AND THE CURRENT BEHAVIOUR IS THE BETTER ONE, which is the strongest reason not to rank it: *** a dropped probe leaves SSR zero with the V bit clear -- a deterministic, DEFINED &#x27;no valid translation&#x27;. Implementing without the manual would replace a defined conservative miss with an INVENTED answer that could steer the guest&#x27;s paging. **That is the same reasoning used to decline `sh4aaalias` before the SH manual arrived -- and that one turned out to be a wrong finding.** The only known consumer prints a line in a debugger display, so a cosmetically wrong DDB line for a human is the entire measured consequence. WORTH ADDING CHEAPLY: one row asserting SSR == 0 after a probe, to pin the DELIBERATE behaviour that today rests on prose in two comments and no oracle at all.">held</span></span></th></tr><tr class="ph st-held"><th scope="row" class="phlabel">Assessment (initial problem)</th><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-16 — CONFIRMED — From R7. After #433 a probe is complained-once and dropped, and the guest then reads regs[CMMU_SSR], which nothing ever writes -- the model writes only PFSR/PFAR (memory_m88k.c:382-405) -- so probes deterministically answer 0, i.e. V-bit clear, a defined &#x27;no valid translation&#x27; rather than a plausible-looking valid answer. The measured OpenBSD/luna88k boot issues NO probes (7 command values, all handled); NetBSD and MP kernels are unmeasured. Real semantics mean reusing the existing translation walk against regs[CMMU_SAR] and synthesising SSR from the header&#x27;s bit definitions (m8820x.h:155-163). No 88200 manual exists in-tree, so where a bit&#x27;s setting condition is not derivable from the header plus the existing walk, leave it 0 and record UNKNOWN. — evidence: _scratchpad/panel_20260815_234456/</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-26 — *** VERDICT: LATENT -- re-file exactly as `gdrompiooddlen` was, and do not rank it live. REACHABILITY MEASURED NEGATIVE WITH CONTROLS IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. *** A full OpenBSD 7.7/luna88k boot to `login:` (7,684,964,995 instructions) issues **SEVEN distinct CMMU commands and ZERO probes**. Denominator stated: 0 of 7 distinct commands, not 0 of 0 -- and it independently replicates #433&#x27;s &#x27;ain 7 of 256&#x27; finding thirty rounds later. **THE CONTROLS ARE WHAT MAKE THE NEGATIVE EVIDENCE:** a real guest supervisor store on a cold debugger, with the planted word DISASSEMBLED BEFORE STEPPING per the hand-assembled-encoding rule -- cmd 0x24 and 0x20 fire the probe detector (POSITIVE), cmd 0x35 does not while still registering as M8CMD_FIRST (NEGATIVE). So the instrument is not a broken grep. CORROBORATING READ that sharpens it beyond &#x27;this guest does not&#x27;: OpenBSD&#x27;s m88k CMMU driver has exactly two CMMU_PROBE writes and **both are inside DDB display routines** -- cmmu_show_translation() and cmmu_cache_state(). **The probe command is a kernel-debugger feature, not an operating path**, reachable only by a human typing at a DDB prompt. It flagged its own caveat: that source is OpenBSD 2.2/mvme88k, the lineage, not the booting guest. *** ON COST, IT ANSWERED THE BRIEF&#x27;S QUESTION AND THEN CORRECTED THE HOLD&#x27;S FRAMING: *** &#x27;needs the translation walk&#x27; is FALSE as a capability claim. m88k_translate_v2p() exists at memory_m88k.c:103 and is ALREADY side-effect-free under FLAG_NOEXCEPTIONS (:344 guards the PG_U/PG_M writeback, :374 returns before any PFSR/PFAR write), its flags already cover the probe&#x27;s selectors (FLAG_INSTR picks cmmu[0]/cmmu[1]; MEMORY_USER_ACCESS is the PROBE_USER/PROBE_SUPER distinction), and the SSR bit layout is in-tree. **And the driving SHAPE is already committed** -- m8820x_sites_probe.py:159 ships a PROBE_SUPER row driven by one real guest instruction, ~3 s, no boot. **This is the sh4dmacie situation in reverse: the shape was already there and nobody re-read the probe.** WHAT IS ACTUALLY MISSING IS AN ORACLE, and it is not small: translate_v2p exposes no BATC-vs- PATC-vs-walk distinction (needed for CMMU_SSR_BH) and none of the U/M/PROT/SO attributes SSR must carry; real probe semantics (does SAR read back the physical address? does a failed probe write PFAR?) are supported only by DDB code reading those registers, which is evidence and not proof; and **there is no 88200/88204 manual in this project.** *** ITS STRONGEST POINT IS THAT THE CURRENT BEHAVIOUR IS THE BETTER ONE: *** a dropped probe leaves SSR zero with the V bit clear -- a deterministic, defined &#x27;no valid translation&#x27;. Implementing without the manual would replace a defined conservative miss with an INVENTED answer that could steer the guest&#x27;s paging. **Same reasoning this project used to decline sh4aaalias before the SH manual arrived -- and that one turned out to be a wrong finding.** It proposed a TRIGGER rather than an indefinite hold, on the SH4_VAL_NCLASS precedent: if an 88200/88204 manual is obtained this becomes a small round. And it suggested one row asserting SSR == 0 after a probe, to pin the DELIBERATE behaviour that today rests on prose in two comments and no oracle at all. — evidence: Agent(model=opus) held-stage seat, same invocation as mrwstore2. BOOTED THE REAL RIG and ran cold-debugger controls; artifacts preserved at _scratchpad/opus_holdq_20260826/.</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-20 — MANUAL — WALL DISCHARGED -- re-fired 2026-08-20 after codex answered a health test (CODEX_ALIVE_20260820, and it got the arithmetic right). Verified a REAL review, not the echo that preceded it: delta over the brief is well past the ~688-byte banner and the usage-limit string is absent from the tail.
