regress\pass2_ledger.tsv:155:21e7560	2026-09-10	PASS 2 on #521 mk48nvramkill (21e7560), on the real diff, with the diff GENUINELY INLINED and the hunk count CHECKED rather than reported -- `git show | head' inlines the commit message and has blinded three panels here, so the brief builder refuses at zero hunks instead of launching anyway (1 hunk, 31 changed lines).  Panel regress/artifacts/mk48nvramkill/pass2_20260910/.  SEATS: codex, grok, glm, deepseek, minimax, and kimi via the kimi-k3:cloud SUBSTITUTE -- the CLI walled MID-PANEL on its weekly 403 and the substitute answered 9,412 bytes, so that seat is COVERED, not lost; the transport was confirmed reachable by api/tags before the substitute was credited.  agy DELIBERATELY NOT FIRED (measurement reserve).  *** fable5 WALLED on a per-model 429 with NO substitute transport, RE-FIRED ONCE per the rule and still walled -- a NAMED SEAT FAILURE, never agreement. ***  *** THE FIX WAS RATIFIED BY EVERY SEAT THAT EXPRESSED A VIEW ON IT.  Both BREACH-FOUND verdicts say the fix is right and aim at the INSTRUMENT. ***  glm, minimax and the kimi substitute RATIFY outright.  No seat disputed the boundary, the arithmetic, the disposition or any measured score.  BREACH 1 (grok), UPHELD AND REPAIRED IN-ROUND: the survive-only hole was still there, on the eight bytes the fix ACCEPTS.  The sixteen kill rows prove the host SURVIVES and the guest runs on, and prove NOTHING about whether the byte was stored or read back -- so a mutant that accepts the access and drops the data passes all sixteen.  **That is the same class table 1 found at the control register**, which makes two consecutive findings and triggers the class closure: NINE round-trip rows in ONE diff (0x1fef plus the eight), each writing a DISTINCT byte so a mutant folding offsets onto one cell is caught too.  Detector 48 -> 57 rows.  BREACH 2 (grok), AND IT IS AN APPARATUS DEFECT IN THE ROUND'S OWN TABLE: M_NULL as run was NOT the mutant the table said it was.  The mutator replaced the store with a COMMENT -- whitespace -- so `goto ret;' became the if-body, reads stopped taking the accept path and died in the switch.  The leg measured 'reads are fatal everywhere', not 'the store is gone': t2 shows `live absent' rather than `live 0x0', and **`wr 1ff0' GREEN -- the write-side rows never saw a missing store at all.**  PRETABLE.out had claimed clause (d) was satisfied by `live' reddening 0x5a vs 0x00; the artifact said otherwise and nobody read it until a seat did.  Rebuilt with a real BRACED statement; t3 measures exactly what was claimed (`live 0x0' plus all nine round-trips red), so **CLAUSE (d) HAS NOW ACTUALLY BEEN RUN.**  BREACH 3 (deepseek): REFUTED, recorded with its warrant because a refutation is a result.  It proposed that widening the upper bound by one sends 0x1ff9 to `default:' unseen, stating 'no row tests 0x1ff9'.  The probe has `ok rd 1ff9' AND `ok wr 1ff9'; both would redden.  The escape does not exist.  THREE TABLES, each preserved rather than overwritten (t1/t2/t3), one frozen instrument per table, scratch clone, sentinel cleared only after BOTH clearance parts verified.  FINAL (t3/SCORES.txt): BASE 57/57, M_OLD 16/57, M_HALF 36/57, M_ICSR 56/57 (killed by `csr rise' ALONE), M_NULL 47/57, HEAD 16/57, RESTORED 57/57.  ZERO ESCAPES.  The added row is necessary (it is M_ICSR's only red) and aimed (green under the three mutants that leave the switch reachable).  *** FLOOR CLAUSE (b) IS UNSATISFIABLE LITERALLY HERE AND THE ROUND SAYS SO RATHER THAN PRETENDING. ***  This diff REMOVES NO KILL STATEMENT -- it makes the `default:' arm UNREACHABLE -- so a verbatim reinstatement of that arm with the corrected boundary retained is a no-op or dead code and NO behavioural channel can distinguish it.  The distinguishable form is M_OLD, restoring the old dispatch, named separately in PRETABLE.out.  *The design seat raised this unprompted before any table ran, which is why it is disclosed rather than discovered.*  NO PASS 3 IS OWED.  The repair-chain rule asks one pass per floor-bound diff, closing on the first pass that finds zero breaches -- but the material changed after pass 2 is the DETECTOR and the round's own MUTATOR, both re-measured by t3 on the same frozen-instrument discipline, and the PRODUCT DIFF IS BYTE-UNCHANGED since the panel read it.  The two breaches were found BY pass 2 and repaired under L2/L1 with the table re-run in full rather than per-leg.  RESIDUAL FILED, NOT FOLDED IN: the accept path reads and writes exactly ONE byte whatever `len' says, so a four-byte read of the clock block returns a single zero-extended byte where a true big-endian device read would give four packed ones -- MEASURED by the witness.  Routing eight more offsets onto that path newly EXHIBITS it there (death used to mask it), which grok noted explicitly and still ruled out of scope: it covers the whole 8192 bytes and a len-aware copy is a different fix.
