regress\selfmutants\diskimage_parse.why:17:LUNA88K and MVME88K.  `sd:` there changes SCSI to... SCSI.  The term only bites on an
doc\intro.html:248:    <li><b><a href="machine_mvme88k.html">Motorola MVME187</a></b> (<a href="machine_mvme88k.html#openbsdmvme88kinstall">OpenBSD/mvme88k</a>)
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:5:  <title>GXemul: MVME88K emulation</title>
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:12:<h1>GXemul: MVME88K emulation</h1>
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:47:<p>This emulation mode attempts to emulate a Motorola MVME187 machine.
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:56:<a name="openbsdmvme88kinstall"></a>
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:57:<h3>OpenBSD/mvme88k:</h3>
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:59:<p>It is possible to run <a href="http://www.openbsd.org/mvme88k.html">OpenBSD/mvme88k</a>
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:60:on an emulated Motorola MVME187 machine in the emulator.
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:62:<p>To install OpenBSD/mvme88k onto an emulated harddisk image, follow these
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:69:	<b>dd if=/dev/zero of=obsd_mvme88k.img bs=1024 count=1 seek=1900000</b>
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:72:  <li>Download the entire mvme88k directory from the ftp server:<pre>
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:73:	<b>wget -np -l 0 -r <a href="https://ftp.nluug.nl/OpenBSD/4.5/mvme88k/">https://ftp.nluug.nl/OpenBSD/4.5/mvme88k/</a></b>
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:81:	<b>mkisofs -o openbsd_mvme88k_4.5.iso -U ftp.nluug.nl/OpenBSD/</b>
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:86:	<b>cp ftp.nluug.nl/OpenBSD/4.5/mvme88k/bsd .
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:91:	<b>gxemul -e mvme187 -d obsd_mvme88k.img -d b:openbsd_mvme88k_4.5.iso -j 4.5/mvme88k/bsd.rd</b>
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:95:	on a real MVME187. There is a problem with finding the filesystem on
doc\machine_mvme88k.html:107:	    root@arzon.gentiane.org:/usr/src/sys/arch/mvme88k/compile/RAMDISK
