regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\opus_p2.md:30:**(1) M_NOVBR — L2, floor breach, repair in-round.** `cr[VBR]` is a field the guarded body reads on the delivery path the seven added labels route through, so it is squarely inside the clause-(d) DEPENDS-ON closure, and dropping it is the canonical *keep the guard, null the repair* form: all seven `implemented = true` and all seven tail labels survive textually and the exception lands at the wrong address. **The probe never writes VBR** (`grep -i vbr` on the frozen probe: one docstring mention, no `stcr cr7`), so VBR is 0 in all twelve rows and `cr[VBR] + 8*vector` is arithmetically indistinguishable from `8*vector`. Guest effect: OpenBSD/mvme88k relocates its vector table, so every one of these seven exceptions would enter at the wrong address on the very guest the fix exists to serve. It is compounded by an **L4 wrong record in two places**: the fallback comment says *"DELIVERED (**VBR** + 8\*vector …)"*, and the probe's clause-(e) contract lists *"a wrong vector base"* among what it **catches** — M_VEC4 and M_VEC7 pin the *scaling*, nothing pins the *base register*.
regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\opus_p2.md:69:**What I could not run:** no gate or battery (forbidden, and `gate_ab`'s oracle is load-sensitive with a panel running); no boot witness, so every claim above about OpenBSD/mvme88k behaviour is derived from the source and the manual, not measured. I did not touch `dev_luna88k.c` or `dev_m8820x.c`. I did not measure per-arm drops for MISALIGNED, UNIMPLEMENTED_OPCODE, PRIVILEGE or ILLEGAL_INTEGER_DIVIDE — M_IMPLOVF is the spot check and each of those four has at least one dedicated row (misalign; unimpl; priv+privtb; div0+dslot), so I am reasoning, not measuring, for those four. **Everything else above that says "measured" names its log in the table.**
