regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\fixreview_20260904\fable5_adjudication.md:8:**VERDICT: GO-WITH-CHANGES.** The FIX is correct block-by-block and refuses NOTHING the one in-tree guest (OpenBSD 2.2/mvme187) does. No previous repair is live-wrong (the one that was -- pass-10's ICLR store-mask claim -- is already reverted). Part 12 finds ZERO floor breaches: all three TxCTL enumeration mutants die. Two cheap, non-design changes gate a valid close: (a) gate-14 has NOT been run on the live probe (`<<GATE14_P12_OWED>>` unfilled; the live probe got a post-table docstring edit, so its 242/242 is inferred, not measured); (b) `pcc2c040kill` is NOT rightly the only HIGH -- `pcc2defaultkill` is an equal host-kill class with more plausible real-boot reachability and is filed severity-untagged.
