regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\fixreview_20260904\codex_gpt6astra_max.err.tail:62:For the real guest, I found no newly refused operation in the inspected OpenBSD paths. The actual guest source exists under `_guest-src-openbsd22`: its [register structure](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_guest-src-openbsd22/sys/arch/mvme88k/dev/pcctworeg.h:1) uses byte fields for these controls and word fields for counters/compares. Its [clock initialization](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_guest-src-openbsd22/sys/arch/mvme88k/dev/clock.c:236) uses those fields and enables COC on **both** timers. This settles the source-reading dispute, but does not establish that ordinary operation produces “both thousands” of pending interrupts. I did not run a guest boot.
