XISTS, PER-SITE, IN THE SOURCE: 51 sites across 12 files already carry a `/* #NNN: was exit(1) */` tag *** -- dev_pvr.c 25, gdrom 5, osiop 5, 8253 4, pcc2 4, and seven more. That is more precise than the per-file tally requested, written at the site, keyed by round, in the fork&#x27;s own tagging ethos. Combined with `census_exits.py --by-file`, which ships and the seat ran, both halves are satisfied. BOUNDED RESIDUAL: nothing answers &#x27;of the 90 ACCESS sites, which already carry a tag?&#x27; -- a one-flag addition (`--tagged`), discharged once, not a standing policy. CONSTRAINT ON THE PREDICATE UNIT, measured and limiting: **the latch idiom is not uniform** -- at least four spellings coexist (struct `warned_*`, function-local `static int warned`, `static int w_warned/r_warned`, and others) -- so a predicate census needs the idiom normalised first, which is separate work and must not be smuggled in. — evidence: Agent(model=opus) held-stage seat, batch B (rule questions). It disclosed FOUR silent empty-set failures in its own apparatus while building these measurements -- a `#define` scan missing re.M reporting 0 of 17,029 macros; `\b` in grep -E returning 2 files where the truth is 12; `[ \t]` in a POSIX bracket not meaning tab; and the documented heredoc backslash-eating -- all caught by the carrier&#x27;s own &#x27;when a count is surprising, open the artifact&#x27; rule.</span></span></td><td class="c ok"><span class="wrap" tabindex="0"><span class="g">✓</span><span class="tip">2026-08-20 — MANUAL — WALL DISCHARGED -- re-fired 2026-08-20 after codex answered a health test (CODEX_ALIVE_20260820, and it got the arithmetic right). Verified a REAL review, not the echo that preceded it: delta over the brief is well past the ~688-byte banner and the usage-limit string is absent from the tail.

