1831:     "note": "SCOPE DEPENDENCY THE #429 DETECTOR RESTS ON AND DOES NOT NAME, found by the review seat: timer_add(idata,...) and timer_update_frequency(d->timer, idata) both survive mutation. My first read was that this re-creates #429; *** reading timer.c REFUTED MY OWN READ *** -- timer_clamp_freq (timer.c:97-110), called at :131 and :199 under #427, clamps, so the effective rate is unchanged.\n\nThe consequence is still real: THE STUBS DO NOT CLAMP, so the detector cannot distinguish 'dev_rtc clamps' from 'timer.c clamps'. R8 advertises itself as asserting 'what the timer core is actually told' while reading last_timer_hz only for IN-RANGE values (1000, 500). #429's detector silently rests on #427 and should say so -- reading last_timer_hz on the three clamp rows makes the dependency explicit.\n\nTHE ONE CASE #427 DOES NOT MASK, also a measured survivor: guarding the update call (`if (idata <= MAX) timer_update_frequency(...)`) -- the guest reads back INT_MAX while the timer runs at its OLD rate, and timer.c is never called at all.",
