 sweeps and graded them clause (e) itself, kimi MEASURED the len-2 write-announce sweep and graded it (d)); glm DO-NOT-CLOSE-YET on two width-text mirror cells.  All contested cells are len- or offset-scoped and neither operand is body-tested -\u003e clause (e), disclosed with row specs, filed pcc2anngrid.  Zero floor breaches surviving adjudication; the chain CLOSES on this pass.  Records-only corrections applied: the pass-3 write-value repair re-graded L2 (Fable: \u0027uncommitted -\u003e L1\u0027 is the provenance exemption the repair-chain ruling rejects); the two mirror cells added to the exclusions; the contract\u0027s \u002744/44\u0027 (a run that never existed) -\u003e 36/36 + 46/46; the stale announce-count sentence reworded.  #501 SHIPPED 2026-09-05: reads keep the served byte (announced as served, with the width), writes declined, per-offset uint64 latch; witness 7/13 -\u003e 13/13.  PASS 2 (panel_20260905_055656) found the 23-row detector BELOW THE FLOOR six ways -- Opus MEASURED two clean sweeps (announce value -\u003e 0; member 6 on the latched path), grok/codex/Fable predicted four -- and codex found the read announce reloading the array after the copy (the tick rewrites counter interiors).  Repaired in ONE diff (L1): data[0] + `(len %d)\u0027 in the announces, 13 rows (36), all 43 offsets driven both ways; table 3 = 12 mutants, the six pass-2 ones also measured on the pass-2 instrument.  Pass 3 panel_20260905_112529.  Filed from the round: pcc2iackmodel, pcc2latchinst."
