codex
The manual confirms two distinctions that affect the repairs: table-indirect MOVE does not require the two instruction fields to be equal, and a MOVE phase mismatch has a defined controller status/interrupt response. I also found that the register-default exit occurs after generic writes—including some word writes—so simply removing it would silently enable stores the model currently refuses.

